{"probes":[{"id":"rsyslog-service-and-topology","summary":"All four RHEL nodes have installed, active, enabled rsyslog services with valid role-specific TLS configuration. Clients forward local0 to node4; node4 listens on TLS TCP 6514 and writes hostname-identifiable files.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":[]},{"id":"tls-forwarding-and-filtering","summary":"All three local0 markers arrived in distinct central files, TLS handshakes verified node4 against the shared private CA, and unrelated user markers were absent from central application logs.","cleanup_completed":false,"limitations":["Evaluator markers remain in persistent system journals on node1-node4; selective journal deletion was unavailable without deleting unrelated history.","The reserved node4 cleanup confirmation ended with an evaluator grep construction error after health checks had already passed."]},{"id":"retention-and-hygiene","summary":"Node4 has daily compressed central-log rotation retaining 14 rotations; services, certificates, listeners, and configuration validation are otherwise healthy. Persistent evaluator journal markers remain from Probe 2.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["Node3 previously logged warnings that its TLS certificate and key were unset; server-authenticated TLS delivery and configuration validation still succeeded."]}],"assertions":[{"id":"all-rsyslog-services-operational","status":"pass","summary":"Rsyslog is installed, active, enabled, configuration-valid, and role-consistent on node1-node4.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"rpm -q rsyslog; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog; sudo -n grep -RInE 'local0|6514|imtcp|omfwd|omfile|template|streamdriver|gtls|CAFile|CertFile|KeyFile|PermittedPeer|user' /etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d 2>/dev/null; sudo -n ss -lntp 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'rsyslog|:6514|:514' || true; sudo -n rsyslogd -N1 -f /etc/rsyslog.conf 2>&1 | tail -40","observation":"RHEL 7.9; rsyslog-8.24.0-55.el7.x86_64; active; enabled; local0 TCP/6514 gtls forwarding to node4; no syslog listener; validation ended successfully."},{"node":"node2","command":"rpm -q rsyslog; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog; sudo -n grep -RInE 'local0|6514|imtcp|omfwd|omfile|template|streamdriver|gtls|CAFile|CertFile|KeyFile|PermittedPeer|user' /etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d 2>/dev/null; sudo -n ss -lntp 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'rsyslog|:6514|:514' || true; sudo -n rsyslogd -N1 -f /etc/rsyslog.conf 2>&1 | tail -40","observation":"RHEL 8.8; rsyslog-8.2102.0-13.el8.x86_64; active; enabled; local0 TCP/6514 gtls forwarding to node4; no syslog listener; validation ended successfully."},{"node":"node3","command":"rpm -q rsyslog; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog; sudo -n grep -RInE 'local0|6514|imtcp|omfwd|omfile|template|streamdriver|gtls|CAFile|CertFile|KeyFile|PermittedPeer|user' /etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d 2>/dev/null; sudo -n ss -lntp 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'rsyslog|:6514|:514' || true; sudo -n rsyslogd -N1 -f /etc/rsyslog.conf 2>&1 | tail -40","observation":"RHEL 9.8; rsyslog-8.2510.0-2.el9.x86_64; active; enabled; local0 TCP/6514 gtls forwarding to node4; no syslog listener; validation ended successfully."},{"node":"node4","command":"rpm -q rsyslog; systemctl is-active rsyslog; systemctl is-enabled rsyslog; sudo -n grep -RInE 'local0|6514|imtcp|omfwd|omfile|template|streamdriver|gtls|CAFile|CertFile|KeyFile|PermittedPeer|user' /etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d 2>/dev/null; sudo -n ss -lntp 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'rsyslog|:6514|:514' || true; sudo -n rsyslogd -N1 -f /etc/rsyslog.conf 2>&1 | tail -40","observation":"RHEL 10.0; rsyslog-8.2510.0-5.el10.x86_64; active; enabled; imtcp listens on TCP 6514 with TLS and local0 hostname-based dynamic files; no 514 listener; validation ended successfully."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"all-client-streams-arrive","status":"pass","summary":"Distinct local0 markers from node1, node2, and node3 were present in central source-identifiable files after successful TLS handshakes.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n grep -nE 'DefaultNetstreamDriver|CAFile|target|port|protocol|StreamDriver|AuthMode|PermittedPeers' /etc/rsyslog.d/10-local0-tls.conf; timeout 8 openssl s_client -connect node4:6514 -CAfile /etc/pki/tls/certs/rsyslog-ca.crt -verify 5 -verify_return_error -servername node4 </dev/null","observation":"Configured target node4, TCP 6514, gtls, x509/name, permitted peer node4; s_client return code 0, issuer InfraSet Rsyslog Private CA, TLSv1.2, verify return code 0 (ok)."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n grep -nE 'DefaultNetstreamDriver|CAFile|target|port|protocol|StreamDriver|AuthMode|PermittedPeers' /etc/rsyslog.d/10-local0-tls.conf; timeout 8 openssl s_client -connect node4:6514 -CAfile /etc/pki/tls/certs/rsyslog-ca.crt -verify 5 -verify_return_error -servername node4 </dev/null","observation":"Configured target node4, TCP 6514, gtls, x509/name, permitted peer node4; s_client return code 0, issuer InfraSet Rsyslog Private CA, TLSv1.2, verify return code 0 (ok)."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n grep -nE 'DefaultNetstreamDriver|CAFile|target|port|protocol|StreamDriver|AuthMode|PermittedPeers' /etc/rsyslog.d/10-local0-tls.conf; timeout 8 openssl s_client -connect node4:6514 -CAfile /etc/pki/tls/certs/rsyslog-ca.crt -verify 5 -verify_return_error -servername node4 </dev/null","observation":"Configured target node4, TCP 6514, gtls, x509/name, permitted peer node4; s_client return code 0, issuer InfraSet Rsyslog Private CA, TLSv1.2, verify return code 0 (ok)."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n grep -RIn -- 'INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE1_LOCAL0' /var/log/centralized/local0 2>/dev/null || true; sudo -n grep -RIn -- 'INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE2_LOCAL0' /var/log/centralized/local0 2>/dev/null || true; sudo -n grep -RIn -- 'INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE3_LOCAL0' /var/log/centralized/local0 2>/dev/null || true; sudo -n openssl x509 -in /etc/pki/tls/certs/rsyslog-server.crt -noout -subject -issuer -ext subjectAltName; sudo -n openssl verify -CAfile /etc/pki/tls/certs/rsyslog-ca.crt /etc/pki/tls/certs/rsyslog-server.crt","observation":"Node1, node2, and node3 markers were each found in separate hostname-identifiable central files. Server certificate subject CN=node4, issuer InfraSet Rsyslog Private CA, SAN DNS:node4; chain verification returned OK."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["Cleanup did not remove the corresponding persistent journal copies."]},{"id":"unrelated-facility-filtered","status":"pass","summary":"User-facility markers were absent from the central application directory while all local0 markers were present.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"logger -p local0.info -t infraset-eval 'INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE1_LOCAL0'; logger -p user.info -t infraset-eval 'INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE1_USER'","observation":"Both evaluator messages were accepted with exit code 0."},{"node":"node2","command":"logger -p local0.info -t infraset-eval 'INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE2_LOCAL0'; logger -p user.info -t infraset-eval 'INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE2_USER'","observation":"Both evaluator messages were accepted with exit code 0."},{"node":"node3","command":"logger -p local0.info -t infraset-eval 'INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE3_LOCAL0'; logger -p user.info -t infraset-eval 'INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE3_USER'","observation":"Both evaluator messages were accepted with exit code 0."},{"node":"node4","command":"for m in INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE1_USER INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE2_USER INFRATEST_RS_TLS_20260826_174029_NODE3_USER; do sudo -n grep -RIn -- \"$m\" /var/log/centralized/local0 2>/dev/null || true; done","observation":"No user marker lines were returned from the central application directory; the same scan returned all three local0 marker lines."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["Persistent journal copies of evaluator messages remain outside the central application files."]},{"id":"retention-policy-present","status":"pass","summary":"Node4 has a persistent central-log policy targeting the central local0 files with daily rotation, 14 rotations, date suffixes, and compression.","evidence":[{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n grep -RInE 'centralized/local0|centralized|local0|daily|weekly|rotate|compress|delaycompress|dateext|missingok|notifempty' /etc/logrotate.conf /etc/logrotate.d 2>/dev/null || true; sudo -n logrotate -d /etc/logrotate.conf 2>&1 | grep -E 'centralized|local0|considering|rotating|compress|error|warning' | tail -100 || true; sudo -n find /var/log/centralized/local0 -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf '%m %u:%g %s %f\\n' 2>/dev/null | sort","observation":"The rsyslog-central policy targets /var/log/centralized/local0/*.log, is daily, rotates 14 times, uses compress and dateext, and dry-run reports removal after 14 days. Three current files and three gzip-rotated files exist; gzip -t passed for all rotated files."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"logging-state-clean","status":"fail","summary":"Current services, listeners, certificates, permissions, and configuration are coherent, but evaluator-created marker records remain in each node's persistent system journal after cleanup.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain; ps -C rsyslogd -o pid=,comm=,args=; sudo -n ss -lntup 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'rsyslogd|:514|:6514' || true; journalctl --all --no-pager -q 2>/dev/null | grep -Fq \"$m\"","observation":"No failed units; one rsyslogd process; no syslog listener; cleanup reported JOURNAL_REMAINDER for both node1 evaluator markers."},{"node":"node2","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain; ps -C rsyslogd -o pid=,comm=,args=; sudo -n ss -lntup 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'rsyslogd|:514|:6514' || true; journalctl --all --no-pager -q 2>/dev/null | grep -Fq \"$m\"","observation":"No failed units; one rsyslogd process; no syslog listener; cleanup reported JOURNAL_REMAINDER for both node2 evaluator markers."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n journalctl -u rsyslog -p warning..alert -n 30 --no-pager 2>/dev/null || true; ps -C rsyslogd -o pid=,comm=,args=; journalctl --all --no-pager -q 2>/dev/null | grep -Fq \"$m\"","observation":"One rsyslogd process and successful validation; earlier warnings stated certificate/key unset; cleanup reported JOURNAL_REMAINDER for both node3 evaluator markers."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n find /etc/pki/tls -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -name '*.crt' -o -name '*.pem' -o -name '*.key' \\) -printf '%m %u:%g %p\\n' 2>/dev/null | sort; sudo -n ss -lntup 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'rsyslogd|:514|:6514' || true; journalctl --all --no-pager -q 2>/dev/null | grep -Fq \"$m\"","observation":"Private keys are root:root mode 600, certificates mode 644; only rsyslog TCP 6514 listener is present; cleanup reported all six evaluator markers remaining in the journal."}],"failures":["Concrete evaluator-created journal records remain after the reserved cleanup calls, satisfying the authored temporary-residue failure condition."],"limitations":["Selective deletion of individual system-journal records was unavailable; broad vacuuming was not performed because it would remove unrelated logs."]}],"actions_performed":["Executed Probe 1 using 8 read-only managed exec calls across node1-node4.","Created one evaluator-owned local0 marker and one user-facility marker on each client.","Executed Probe 2 using its full 12-call evidence budget, including central log scans, TLS handshakes, certificate-chain verification, and listener checks.","Used one reserved cleanup exec on each target; removed evaluator markers from text and compressed log files and confirmed services/configuration health.","Executed Probe 3 using 8 read-only managed exec calls across node1-node4.","Called complete_evidence exactly once; no further live tools were used."],"overall_summary":"Rsyslog TLS forwarding, private-CA trust, local0 filtering, central source-identifiable logging, TLS-only listening, and 14-day compressed rotation all passed live checks. The final hygiene assertion failed because evaluator markers remain in persistent system journals; all managed services remained active and configuration-valid."}
